#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# confirm

#% text
# `confirm(x)` gives `x`, unless it is a failure or `missing(...)`: then `failure(confirmation_failed, x)` is thrown to the enclosing `enclose`. `confirm(x, info)` evaluates `info` (held until then) before throwing; `confirm(x, info, tag)` throws to an `enclose` with that tag. A failure that no `enclose` catches stays the failure it is.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
enclose(f(x, confirm(y), z))
#% output
#= f(x, y, z)

#% cell
enclose(confirm(missing()) + 2)
#% output
#! failure(confirmation_failed, missing())

#% cell
enclose(g(3 + confirm(2, null, "t")), identity, "t")
#% output
#= g(5)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `enclose`, `throw`, `catch`, `is_failure`
